om/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50577602/sec-consider-termination-lsu-membership","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia defensive coordinator Glenn Schumann agrees to coach Florida State","description":"Georgia's Glenn Schumann, one of the country's top defensive coordinators and part of a staff that has the Bulldogs at No. 1 in the CFP rankings, agreed to a five-year deal to become the next coach at Florida State, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-24T02:51:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577665/uga-defensive-coordinator-schumann-coach-florida-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aiden Flora, nation's leading rusher, re-signs with Iowa State for next season","description":"Iowa State running back Aiden Flora, who leads the nation in rushing, announced Monday that he has re-signed with the Cyclones for next season.","published":"2026-11-23T23:57:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577520/aiden-flora-nation-leading-rusher-re-signs-iowa-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas A&M names John Thornton interim athletic director effective Dec. 1","description":"John Thornton will take over as interim athletic director at Texas A&M, effective Dec. 1, replacing the departed Trev Alberts.","published":"2026-11-23T22:07:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576559/texas-names-john-thornton-interim-ad-effective-dec-1","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Giants DC Dennard Wilson interviews for HC job at alma mater Maryland","description":"Giants defensive coordinator Dennard Wilson had a virtual interview recently for the vacant head coaching job at Maryland, sources told NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-23T21:22:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575838/sources-giants-dennard-wilson-interviews-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU's Lane Kiffin apologizes for using profanity during halftime interview","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin has apologized for using profanity during a halftime interview with the school's radio network in Saturday's loss to Tennessee.","published":"2026-11-23T20:12:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575735/lsu-kiffin-apologizes-use-profanity-interview","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest leading rusher Ty Clark ruled out for season","description":"Wake Forest running back Ty Clark will miss the rest of the season, coach Jake Dickert announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T20:30:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575731/wake-forest-leading-rusher-ry-clark-ruled-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Syracuse rules QB Steve Angeli (shoulder) out vs. Notre Dame","description":"Syracuse has ruled starting quarterback Steve Angeli out for Saturday's game against Notre Dame due to a shoulder injury.","published":"2026-11-23T18:40:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575118/syracuse-rules-qb-steve-angeli-shoulder-vs-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana not yet naming starting QB for game vs. Purdue, Curt Cignetti says","description":"Indiana is not yet naming a starting quarterback for Saturday's rivalry game against Purdue, coach Curt Cignetti said Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T18:51:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575086/indiana-not-yet-naming-starting-qb-game-vs-purdue","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama's Kalen DeBoer expects QB Keelon Russell to be 'full go' vs. Auburn","description":"Alabama coach Kalen DeBoer said Monday that he expects QB Keelon Russell, who is working his way back from an ankle injury, to be \"full go\" for rivalry week against Auburn.","published":"2026-11-23T18:13:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50574915/alabama-deboer-expects-qb-russell-full-go-auburn","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5077638/bray-hubbard","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bray_Hubbard"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Bray Hubbard","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bray_Hubbard","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:43Z","intro":"Brayson \"Bray\" Hubbard (born February 14, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Alabama Crimson Tide.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Hubbard was born in Ocean Springs, Mississippi and attended Ocean Springs High School. He was rated as a three-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Alabama Crimson Tide over offers from FAU, Mississippi State, Navy, Tulane, and Southern Miss."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman in 2023, Hubbard appeared in nine games for Alabama, notching one tackle. In week 8 of the 2024 season, he notched nine tackles in a 24–17 loss to Tennessee, after replacing injured starter Keon Sabb. Heading into week 9, Hubbard was named the team's starting safety due to Sabb's injury. In his first career start, he totaled seven tackles and an interception in a win over Missouri. Hubbard went viral for jogging during a play that resulted in a touchdown versus Florida State in 2025."}]}}